4. Failure Case
The system may misclassify homeless encampments with trash as purely environmental issues.
This can result in incorrect routing and inappropriate response from city departments.
5. Oversight and Tradeoff
Human review is required for edge cases such as homeless encampments mixed with waste. These cases are flagged for manual inspection by city staff instead of being fully automated.
The tradeoff is that adding human oversight slows down response time and reduces full automation efficiency, but it improves fairness, accuracy, and prevents misrouting sensitive social issues.
